---
code: K0033
title: Bad Element Id
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, ui-element, id]
description: "UI element ':id' must be a valid kebab-case identifier"
---

A UI element ID—passed as the first argument to an element using a leading colon (`:id`)—must be a valid lowercase/kebab-case identifier (`:my-button`). Missing names, uppercase names, keywords, or non-identifier tokens after `:` are invalid.

## Example

This error occurs when `:` in the first element argument position is not followed by a valid identifier:

```kura
fn header() =>
  #text(:123, "Title")

fn footer() =>
  #text(:, "Footer")
```

## Solution

Follow `:` with a valid kebab-case identifier as the first argument to the UI element:

```kura
fn header() =>
  #text(:page-title, "Title")
```
